      "content": "curiosity feels like a lot of work for something that's just gonna end in nothingness anyway. if the end result is always the same, why go through the exhaustion of the middle part? it just seems like there's more peace in just letting go of the struggle altogether. doesn't it seem more rational to just stop the cycle when you realize it's meaningless?",
